    <h2>The Garden of the Second Conjugation</h2>
    <p class="story">A moonlit garden of roses. Statues whisper <b>-ēre</b> verbs: <em>videō, moneō, habeō, teneō…</em> Each statue holds a piece of the last key. Answer them all before the moon sets!</p>

    <div class="q" id="q4a">
      <p class="qtext">1 · The first statue asks: which infinitive belongs to the SECOND conjugation?</p>
      <div class="choices">
        <button class="choice" data-ok="0">amāre</button>
        <button class="choice" data-ok="1">monēre</button>
        <button class="choice" data-ok="0">portāre</button>
        <button class="choice" data-ok="0">laudāre</button>
      </div>
      <button class="hintbtn">Need a hint?</button><div class="hinttext">2nd conjugation infinitives end in <b>-ēre</b> (long e), 1st in <b>-āre</b>.</div>
      <p class="feedback"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="q" id="q4b">
      <p class="qtext">2 · Two statues stare at the stars. Type the Latin for "they see" (from <span class="latin">vidēre</span>).</p>
      <div class="typein"><input type="text" aria-label="answer" placeholder="vid…"><button class="check">Check</button></div>
      <button class="hintbtn">Need a hint?</button><div class="hinttext">Take the stem <b>vide-</b> and add <b>-nt</b>.</div>
      <p class="feedback"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="q" id="q4c">
      <p class="qtext">3 · A statue proudly declares: <span class="latin">"Habēmus rosās!"</span> What does <span class="latin">habēmus</span> mean?</p>
      <div class="choices">
